content:
{
  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent hemoglobin eligibility threshold: inclusion criterion 11 states ≥9 g/dL but parenthetical allows >8 g/dL for gastric/gastroesophageal cancer, which is contradictory and not clearly justified.",
      "page": 44,
      "quote": "Hemoglobin ≥ 9 g/dL. NOTE: Patients requiring ongoing transfusions or growth factor support to maintain hemoglobin ≥9 g/dL are not eligible. (> 8 g/dL in Gastric Cancer / Gastroesophageal Cancer Indications)",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inclusion criterion 12 washout for hormonal therapy is ambiguous: 'mBC' is undefined and the phrase '≥ 3 weeks (≥ 2 weeks or 5 half-lives...' is confusing, potentially allowing shorter washout than stated.",
      "page": 45,
      "quote": "Anti-cancer chemotherapy (Immunotherapy [non-antibody-based therapy]), retinoid therapy, mBC; hormonal therapy: ≥ 3 weeks (≥ 2 weeks or 5 half-lives, whichever is longer, for small-molecule targeted agents such as 5-fluorouracil-based agents, folinate agents or weekly paclitaxel; ≥ 6 weeks for nitrosureas or mitomycin C).",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Exclusion criterion 4 uses different QTcF thresholds for males and females, but the protocol does not specify sex-specific correction elsewhere; this is not an error per se, but the threshold for males (>450 msec) is stricter than standard and may be inconsistent with other sections.",
      "page": 47,
      "quote": "Corrected QT interval by Fridericia's formula (QTcF) prolongation to > 470 msec (females) or > 450 msec (males) based on average of the screening triplicate 12-lead ECG.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inclusion criterion 7 requires an FFPE tumor sample but states 'fine needle aspirates are inadequate' – this is a contradiction because fine needle aspirates can be FFPE; the intent is likely that cytology specimens are inadequate, but the wording is confusing.",
      "page": 44,
      "quote": "All patients must provide an existing FFPE tumor sample for retrospective central HER2 testing. ... Specimens with limited tumor content and fine needle aspirates are inadequate for defining tumor HER2 mutation status.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inclusion criterion 11 lists 'INR/PT, and either PTT or aPTT' but the abbreviation 'PTT' is not defined in the table footnote; only aPTT is defined, which may cause confusion.",
      "page": 45,
      "quote": "INR/PT, and either PTT or aPTT",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inclusion criterion 13a requires a serum pregnancy test at screening and urine test prior to each IP administration, but the protocol does not specify the frequency of urine tests or whether they are needed at every cycle; this is a minor omission.",
      "page": 45,
      "quote": "For women of childbearing potential, a negative result for serum pregnancy test (test must have a sensitivity of at least 25 mIU/mL) must be available at the screening visit and urine beta-human chorionic gonadotropin pregnancy test prior to each administration of IP.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inclusion criterion 14 requires contraception for 7 months after last dose, but the protocol does not specify the half-life of T-DXd to justify this duration; this is not an error but a missing justification.",
      "page": 46,
      "quote": "must agree to continue using such precautions for at least 7 months after the last dose of IP.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Exclusion criterion 1 excludes HER2-overexpressing breast/gastric/gastroesophageal cancer, but inclusion criterion 6 allows patients with those tumor types if they have specific HER2 mutations; the exclusion is conditional on overexpression, which is consistent, but the wording 'Patients with breast, gastroesophageal and gastric cancer harboring selected specific HER2 activating mutations ... will be eligible if HER2 is not overexpressed' is redundant and could be misinterpreted.",
      "page": 47,
      "quote": "HER2 overexpressing (IHC3+ or IHC2+/ISH+) adenocarcinoma of breast, gastric or gastroesophageal junction as determined by local HER2 testing. Patients with breast, gastroesophageal and gastric cancer harboring selected specific HER2 activating mutations (See inclusion criteria 6) and who have received prior trastuzumab or other HER2 targeting therapy will be eligible if HER2 is not overexpressed (IHC3+ or IHC2+/ISH+) in in a tissue biopsy taken after documented disease progression following trastuzumab and/or HER2 targeting treatment.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Exclusion criterion 6 prohibits pleural effusion, ascites, or pericardial effusion that requires drainage, but inclusion criterion 11 does not mention effusions; this is not a contradiction but a potential inconsistency with the patient population (some tumor types may have effusions).",
      "page": 47,
      "quote": "Has a pleural effusion, ascites or pericardial effusion that requires drainage, peritoneal shunt, or Cell-free and Concentrated Ascites Reinfusion Therapy (CART).",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Exclusion criterion 16 allows patients with treated brain metastases but requires a minimum of 2 weeks between whole brain radiotherapy and enrolment; however, inclusion criterion 12 requires a 4-week washout for radiation therapy to the chest, but not for brain; this is not a direct contradiction but may be inconsistent.",
      "page": 48,
      "quote": "A minimum of 2 weeks must have elapsed between the end of whole brain radiotherapy and study enrolment.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "The protocol does not specify the total duration of the study or the expected enrolment period, which is a missing element for a clinical trial protocol.",
      "page": 39,
      "quote": "Approximately 100 patients will be treated in this study with a maximum of approximately 20 patients per tumor type",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "The protocol does not include a statistical analysis section (e.g., sample size calculation, analysis populations, handling of missing data) in the provided excerpt, which is a critical omission for a protocol.",
      "page": 37,
      "quote": "Table 8 shows the objectives and endpoints for this study.",
      "severity": "critical"
    }
  ]
}
